x cut on  average if you're making eighty five  thousand bucks a year you get a twenty  percent tax cut 165 thousand bucks a  year you get an eight percent tax cut so  the benefit is really focused on the  middle class and those who are in this  range of you know thirty to seventy  thousand bucks senator there is an  argument for corporate tax cuts and it's  that they will reinvest and pass those  savings on to middle-class Americans but  the Tax Policy Center said it could take  up to twenty years why will it take so  much time to put money back in employees  pockets yeah I think every economist who  looks at it says that we've got to  change the way we tax our companies  because they can't be competitive and  that some of the benefit is going to go  directly to workers now people disagree  some say that's 80% of the benefits some  say it's 25% of the benefit but you're  right that seem to go to families and  working families across America  I think it'll happen very quickly I know  there is a one-year delay in the  corporate cuts and there is an immediate  cut for families but I do think during  that time period because expensing will  be something that a lot of companies  will take advantage of immediate  expensing I think there'll be a lot of  investment  and that's what the economists seem to  say so I can't understand why it would  take that long because I think what  you'll see is immediate decisions made  by companies knowing they're going to  have this ability to be able to invest  more increase productivity and get wages  back up do you think it was appropriate  for President Trump to call one of your  colleagues senator Warren pocahontas  well you know they have a back-and-forth  that I'm gonna stay out of it it's a  long-standing I think that event  yesterday was an event to honor an  incredible achievement which was these  Navajo code talkers and should have  focused on that and you know what they  did in World War two is truly  spectacular and you know